Recoil [
    Title: "Loos parameter ids"
    Description: {
        The one place Loos's parameter ordering is written down.

        The editor names these ids in its layout block; the headless layout
        check re-declares that block and must resolve the same names to the
        same numbers, or it would confirm a layout nobody ships. Importing
        the editor itself is not an option -- it carries a `foreign <loos.h>`
        block and its whole body, neither of which a windowless check can
        link. A module of nothing but an enum can be imported anywhere, for
        the same reason editor-size.rcl can.
    }
    Type: module
    Module: examples/pokuston/loos/editor-params
    Exports: [Param!]
]

; Order is the ABI: these are the indices loos_get_parameter and
; loos_parameter_default are called with, so a variant may only be appended --
; except across a state-schema break, which is what removing the four filter
; envelope stages was. Schema 2 renumbers, and loos-load-state refuses schema 1
; rather than reading the old ids as though they still meant something.
Param!: make enum! [
    cutoff resonance env-amount
    attack decay sustain release
    lfo-rate lfo-cutoff-depth morph
]
